Clave-Orbit

Creative Catalyst: It was reverse-engineered from a corrupted cassette found in a time capsule.

Clave-Orbit sounds like a razor-sharp collision between gravity and grease. The percussive, aggressive snap of Drill 808s acts as the "hull" of the song, while the Hohner Clavinet—fed through liquid-helium oscillators and pitch-shifting debris—creates a shimmering, celestial hum that defies terrestrial physics. It is the sound of an orbital station rusting in deep space while the bassline fractures the windows.

Genre DNA
*   Tempo & Pulse: 142–148 BPM, defined by stuttering, polymetric hi-hat triplets that drag against the "weightless" float of the Clavinet chords.
*   Harmonic Palette: Dissonant Microtonal Gamelan scales layered over "Event Horizon" minor triads, often using inverted dominant sevenths that resolve upward into static.
*   Production Signatures: "Bit-Rot Percussion" (layering digital clipping into the kick drum), "Orbital Filtering" (LFOs tied to real-time telemetry data), and "Tungsten Clavs" (physical modeling of strings stretched to breaking point).
*   Dynamics: A violent "Pressure Collapse"—tracks start with claustrophobic density and expand into thin, terrifying atmospheric vacuums, only to be crushed by the percussion again.

Scene & Origin Lore
The subculture surfaced in the derelict "Deep-Sector 9" refueling depots, where scavengers discovered the "Corrupted Cassette." Fashion is defined by pressurized flight suits worn with mismatched streetwear, accessorized with shards of leaded glass hung from throat-chains. Their primary ritual, the "Sync-Burn," involves vibrating Hohner Clavinets in unison to force the playback of the distorted cassette until the frequencies stabilize, a process that frequently causes localized electrical outages and visual hallucinations in the participants.

Instruments: Hohner Clavinet (heavily processed), Custom 808-Sub Modular Synthesizer, "Gravity-String" Harps (tension-sensitive controllers), and Field Recordings of Ionosphere static.

For Fans Of: Burial, Flying Lotus, Oneohtrix Point Never, and 808 State.

